<p style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"> </p>
<HR SIZE="3" style="COLOR:#999999" WIDTH="100%" ALIGN="CENTER">
<h5 align="left"><a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a></h5>


<Center><DIV STYLE="width:8.5in" align="left">
 <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Dear Fellow DBV Shareholders, </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">At DBV, our mission remains steadfast in addressing the real-world needs of families with children living with life-threatening food allergies who are
actively seeking treatment options. In a context of a shift in the landscape of allergy management, moving from a passive approach of avoidance to an active and targeted treatment strategy, DBV is well positioned to play a pivotal role as a key
component in the allergists&#146; toolkit for managing food allergy. To accomplish this, we remain focused on three pillars: safety, efficacy, and ease of use with a target population of peanut-allergic children aged 1 through 7 years old. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The publication of our EPITOPE study in the prestigious New England Journal of Medicine (NEJM) was a significant achievement in 2023. The publication of this
groundbreaking study, focused on peanut-allergic toddlers aged 1 through 3 <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">years-old,</FONT> underscores the significance and importance of our product and its potential. Notably, the study data shows that 67% of
subjects treated with Viaskin<SUP STYLE="font-size:75%; vertical-align:top">&#153;</SUP> Peanut 250 &micro;g met response criteria after 12 months, compared to 33.5% in the placebo arm. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Late last year, DBV had the opportunity to give a late-breaking presentation, at the American College of Allergy, Asthma&nbsp;&amp; Immunology (ACAAI), of the
EPITOPE open-label extension. Highlighted in that presentation was a <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">24-month</FONT> readout of the interim data which showed a continued benefit of long-term treatment with Viaskin Peanut. Significantly, 56% of
children in the open-label extension were able to consume an equivalent of <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">12-14</FONT> peanuts without experiencing an allergic reaction during the <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">year-two</FONT> food challenge.
Moreover, 81% achieved an increase in eliciting dose from a median of 100mg (the equivalent of approximately 1/3 of a peanut) to <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">3-4</FONT> peanuts. We view this data as being highly meaningful and motivating to our
continued mission to bring Viaskin Peanut to market. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">In 2023, we launched the VITESSE study, focusing on safety and efficacy in 4 through <FONT
STYLE="white-space:nowrap">7-year-olds,</FONT> recognizing this is an age group where children&#146;s lifestyle involves an increase in social interactions, school, and extracurricular activities. As an update, enrollment is ongoing and we expect to
screen the last subject in VITESSE in 2024. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">As the typical age of diagnosis for a peanut allergy in children is between the ages of 1 through 5 years
old, we believe that initiating immunotherapy with Viaskin Peanut in children 1 through 7 is optimal. Parents are highly motivated to seek treatment upon diagnosis. We strive to protect peanut allergic children in this age group from accidental
peanut consumption and hope to provide greater peace of mind for the children and all their loved ones. The three pillars of Viaskin Peanut: safety, efficacy, and ease of use without restrictions on daily life, are intended to achieve that outcome.
Furthermore, as our data shows, and like other immunotherapies with the potential to reeducate the immune system, the earlier treatment is initiated, the better the clinical outcome, as the immune system is particularly susceptible to being
reeducated in early life. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">DBV continues to expand a substantial clinical dataset, with already close to 1,700 children on active treatment across age
groups when we combine data from our prior Phase 3 trials, including approximately 600 toddlers aged 1 through 3 years and 1,100 children aged 4 through 7. We are accumulating the largest ever cumulative exposure to an investigational product in
pediatric food allergy. More than one million Viaskin Peanut patches have been applied to peanut-allergic children in our trials&#151;which is the equivalent to more than one million days of therapy. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Based on the number of children on active treatment, Viaskin Peanut is clearly a well-studied therapeutic, which gives us confidence in the potential of
Viaskin as a novel treatment option and the science of epicutaneous immunotherapy as a platform. The allergist community and patient advocacy groups are emphatic in their support of Viaskin Peanut as a treatment option and are eager to welcome it
when it is approved and becomes commercially available. Therefore, we are dedicating all our efforts towards filing parallel Biologic License Applications (BLAs) in 1 through <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">3-year-olds</FONT> and 4 through <FONT
STYLE="white-space:nowrap">7-year-olds,</FONT> reflecting our mission to advancing treatment options for young children living with peanut allergy. </P>
</DIV></Center>


<p style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"> </p>
<HR SIZE="3" style="COLOR:#999999" WIDTH="100%" ALIGN="CENTER">
<h5 align="left"><a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a></h5>


<Center><DIV STYLE="width:8.5in" align="left">
 <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">To accomplish this, our commitment to financial discipline and focused spending remains a cornerstone of our
culture and <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">day-to-day</FONT></FONT> life. We appreciate the support and confidence of our shareholders so that we may continue to prioritize the completion of our studies for Viaskin
Peanut. The PIPE and ATM offerings conducted in 2022 and 2023 allowed us to fuel Viaskin Peanut development progress in 2023. More than 90% of our expenditures and efforts are directed toward operations for Viaskin Peanut&#146;s clinical development
and preparing for BLA filings. With a cash balance of $141&nbsp;million at <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">year-end</FONT> 2023, we will continue to employ the requisite financial discipline necessary to give us the ability to further advance
Viaskin Peanut development throughout the year. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">While Viaskin Peanut is our near-term priority program, our belief in epicutaneous immunotherapy as a
platform is reflected in the Viaskin Milk program which is being readied to advance to Phase 2b for both cow&#146;s milk allergy and cow&#146;s milk induced eosinophilic esophagitis (EoE). In addition, we continue to investigate the potential
application of Viaskin in other immunologic indications with a high unmet need, such as celiac disease. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Our mission-driven focus centers on people living
with food allergies and other immunologic conditions with significant unmet medical need. We are building a future with more options and better outcomes for these people and their families. We are grateful for the ongoing support from our
shareholders in realizing this vision. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">In closing, I wish to state that we believe our current stock price undervalues our company and does not reflect
the potential of Viaskin Peanut. We remain steadfast in our efforts to bring Viaskin Peanut to market. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Thank you for your belief in DBV Technologies and
its future. </P> <P STYLE="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="40%" BORDER="0" STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt">


